Kind: ablation
Issue: #781
Takes out: the write of CSTAR -- syscall_init() leaves it as reset left it, which under KVM and TCG is zero, as it was on every processor before #781.
Accel: tcg,kvm
Run: --entry 0 300 -smp 4
Expect: processor [0-9]+: its system-call registers are not what syscall_init\(\) writes: CSTAR 0x0+,
Note: the census's line for a processor whose CSTAR reads zero; the summary line says WRONG too, but this one names the register and the value.

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/syscall/syscall.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/syscall/syscall.c
index 021a359c..2a65c179 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/syscall/syscall.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/x86_64/syscall/syscall.c
@@ -660,7 +660,6 @@ void syscall_init(void)
 	 * SYSENTER faults while IA32_SYSENTER_CS is zero, and only then --
 	 * so it is made zero rather than found zero.
 	 */
-	wrmsr(MSR_CSTAR, w.cstar);
 	wrmsr(MSR_SYSENTER_CS, w.sysenter_cs);
 	wrmsr(MSR_SYSENTER_ESP, w.sysenter_esp);
 	wrmsr(MSR_SYSENTER_EIP, w.sysenter_eip);
